{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ohqktu","slide":1,"text":"CORE MESSAGE: Judges, we built Continuum because compliance should not disappear after a user passes onboarding.\nOpen warmly: “Imagine approving a user today, then discovering tomorrow that their credential was revoked while their asset kept moving. Continuum closes that gap.”\n[Sources]\n- Internal workspace: product specification, demo script, deployment record (2026-08-03).\n- User-provided Continuum logo.\n[/Sources]"}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/c8szka","slide":2,"title":"A QUESTION FOR THE JUDGES","textShapes":16}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/0f21gnq5","slide":2,"text":"A QUESTION FOR THE JUDGES","textPreview":"A QUESTION FOR THE JUDGES","textChars":25,"textLines":1,"bbox":[72,45,740,24]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/zet07ipk","slide":2,"text":"What happens after a verified user becomes ineligible?","textPreview":"What happens after a verified user becomes ineligible?","textChars":54,"textLines":1,"bbox":[72,80,1080,90]}
